{"clock":73,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794311873,"data":{"issue":"a9942a368e7ba640b3b6e0b02898656fbc3a5bad","forge_id":"6208108486","number":"87","url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/87"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794311873,"data":{"issue":"a9942a368e7ba640b3b6e0b02898656fbc3a5bad","field":"title","value":"cli: @me without a forge: resolve to the person you write as"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794311873,"data":{"issue":"a9942a368e7ba640b3b6e0b02898656fbc3a5bad","field":"body","value":"Found writing the user manual (PR #86).\n\n**Now.** `@me` in a filter or an assignment means your *forge login*. On a board that never synced with a forge, `git board set \u003cid\u003e assignee=+@me` and `ls \"involves:@me\"` fail: \"@me needs your forge login\". For a product whose point is independence from forges, that's backwards.\n\n**Want.** `@me` resolves to the person you write as (`board.me`): their forge login where they have one on the issue's forge, else their name. Assignee labels on a forge-less board name people by name (`assignee:ada`), and the sync maps a name to the forge login when the person has an account there.\n\n**Acceptance.** On a fresh board with no forge: `git board me --new`, then `set \u003cid\u003e assignee=+@me` and `ls involves:@me` work; after a GitHub sync, the label maps to the GitHub login.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794311873,"data":{"issue":"a9942a368e7ba640b3b6e0b02898656fbc3a5bad","field":"status","value":"closed"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794311873,"data":{"issue":"a9942a368e7ba640b3b6e0b02898656fbc3a5bad","field":"labels","value":"feat"}}]}